WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
- I mentioned, you won
a Grammy for your work

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.180
with your girlfriend, Taylor Swift.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.029
(audience cheers)

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:04.862
So that's amazing.

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:06.027
- Thank you.

00:00:06.027 --> 00:00:08.760
- But I love that you,
I find it really cool

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.714
You did it under a pseudonym.
You, it, wasn't your name.

00:00:10.714 --> 00:00:11.820
- Yeah.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.149
- Why did you choose to do that?

00:00:13.149 --> 00:00:15.270
- Well, I chose, we chose
to do it so that people

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.070
first and foremost would
listen to the music first

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.820
before dissecting the fact
that we did it together.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.653
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:23.434
- But um, yeah it did it
under a name William Bowery.

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:24.510
- Yeah

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.400
- Which sounds like

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.233
- Very fancy

00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:27.706
- Very fancy. Sounds like a kind of

00:00:27.706 --> 00:00:31.250
Agatha Christie character
should be wearing a monocle

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.732
with a big mustache, but it was

00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:37.970
yeah, it was a combination
of William who my

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.150
great grandfather who I
never actually met was

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.600
a composer. He wrote a
lot of classical music

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.290
and he wrote a lot of film scores.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:50.290
And then Bowery is the area
in New York that I spent a lot

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.710
of time in when I first
went over there. So..

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.543
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:00:53.543 --> 00:00:54.376
- Stick them together.

00:00:54.376 --> 00:00:55.840
- [Kelly] That's how you do, okay.

